WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Anterior View of Human Heart Anatomy: 3D Functional Overview.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The heart is a muscular organ located in the middle mediastinum, enclosed within the fibroserous pericardial sac.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Examining the sternocostal anterior surface: The right ventricle forms approximately two-thirds of the anterior cardiac surface.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Notice the anterior interventricular sulcus marking the boundary between right and left ventricles, carrying the LAD artery.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Superiorly, observe the ascending aorta and pulmonary trunk arising from the cardiac base, arching over the pulmonary bifurcations.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:01.000
The superior vena cava drains venous blood from upper extremities and head directly into the right atrium.
